{
  "desc": "Invite links: make = shareUrl (JS) / InviteLink.Make (C#) / OneLobbyInvite.make (GDScript), parse = codeFromUrl / InviteLink.Parse / OneLobbyInvite.parse. make: a lobby code (6 Crockford characters, any spelling normalizeCode takes) and an absolute http(s) base give base with the param (default \"join\") removed and set last as the display code with a hyphen (7HQ-4K2); the fragment is kept, a missing path becomes \"/\", the scheme and host are lower-cased, and every other query entry is re-encoded as application/x-www-form-urlencoded (space = +, a key without = gets an empty value). A bad code or a base that is not absolute http(s) is an error (JS throws, C# ArgumentException, GDScript returns \"\"). parse: the first param entry in the query (else, only when the query has no such key, in the fragment) read as application/x-www-form-urlencoded, then normalized; null (GDScript: \"\") when there is none or it is not a code. Text is not cleaned beyond trimming surrounding whitespace: a trailing dot or angle brackets make the code invalid. Join codes of direct lobbies are not invite-link codes.",
